{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q419861","formula":"C₉H₁₁BrN₂O₅","hill":"C9H11BrN2O5","elements":["H","C","N","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":9.0,"H":11.0,"N":2.0,"O":5.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"Bromodeoxyuridine","ru":"Бромдезоксиуридин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Bromodeoxyuridine (5-bromo-2'-deoxyuridine, BrdU, BUdR, BrdUrd, broxuridine) is a synthetic nucleoside analogue with a chemical structure similar to thymidine. BrdU is commonly used to study cell proliferation in living tissues and has been studied as a radiosensitizer and diagnostic tool in people with cancer. During the S phase of the cell cycle (when DNA replication occurs), BrdU can be incorporated in place of thymidine in newly synthesized DNA molecules of dividing cells.","ru":"Бромдезоксиуридин (5-бромо-2'-дезоксиуридин) (англ. Bromodeoxyuridine), сокращённо БДУ (англ. BrdU) — синтетический нуклеозид, аналог тимидина, используемый для выявления пролиферирующих клеток в живых тканях, для изучения репликации ДНК, для дифференциальной окраски сестринских хроматид."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":6035,"mass":307.1,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1[C@@H]([C@H](O[C@H]1N2C=C(C(=O)NC2=O)Br)CO)O","inchikey":"WOVKYSAHUYNSMH-RRKCRQDMSA-N","iupac":"5-bromo-1-[(2R,4S,5R)-4-hydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)oxolan-2-yl]pyrimidine-2,4-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6035","atoms":28,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.579,"y":-2.868,"z":0.345,"el":"Br"},{"x":1.606,"y":-0.176,"z":-0.997,"el":"O"},{"x":3.846,"y":1.575,"z":0.139,"el":"O"},{"x":2.28,"y":-2.869,"z":-0.619,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.116,"y":2.858,"z":-0.363,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.362,"y":-0.343,"z":0.217,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.434,"y":0.633,"z":-0.185,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.722,"y":1.247,"z":-0.074,"el":"N"},{"x":3.048,"y":0.555,"z":0.737,"el":"C"},{"x":0.965,"y":0.915,"z":-0.321,"el":"C